{"name":"Stage Whisper","hex":"#d8d9ca","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stage whisper","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A line that is performed on stage as if it were whispered, but is spoken loud enough for the audience to hear.","Any loud whisper intended to be overheard."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To perform a stage whisper."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stage_whisper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stage Whisper","blocks":[{"text":"Stage Whisper is the first compilation album by British-French singer & actress Charlotte Gainsbourg, released on December 13, 2011 by Because Music & Elektra Records."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/dc/Stage_Whisper_-_Charlotte_Gainsbourg_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stage_Whisper"},{"title":"Whispering","blocks":[{"text":"Whispering is an unvoiced mode of phonation in which the vocal cords are abducted so that they do not vibrate; air passes between the arytenoid cartilages to create audible turbulence during speech. Supralaryngeal articulation remains the same as in normal speech."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whispering"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Two_Girls%2C_Tigray_%2814991776680%29.jpg/500px-Two_Girls%2C_Tigray_%2814991776680%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Two_Girls%2C_Tigray_%2814991776680%29.jpg/500px-Two_Girls%2C_Tigray_%2814991776680%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A girl whispers to another girl.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATwo_Girls%2C_Tigray_(14991776680).jpg"}],"sounds":{"stage whisper":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/56/En-us-stage_whisp